    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d44">

                <pb facs="0133" n="31" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg31"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.51/571: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Geissler</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-04-08T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 8, 1927—3
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>22. Department’s 5, January 24, 6 p.m., your despatch 1401, January 27.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d44-f1"/></p>
                <p>Following reply has been made to British Ambassador’s request for good
                        offices:<anchor n="4" xml:id="d44-f2"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“While the Government of the United States cannot undertake to advise the
                            Guatemalan Government regarding its action with respect to the specific
                            proposal understood to have been made by the bondholders, I am
                            instructing the American Minister to assist in any proper way in
                            arriving at a satisfactory adjustment of the matter, and to inform the
                            Guatemalan Government that the Government of the United States would be
                            glad to see a suitable settlement in the interest of both parties.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <pb facs="0134" n="32" xml:id="pg32"/>
                <p>[Paraphrase.] In carrying out this instruction you should be very careful to make
                    no formal representations. You should restrict yourself to indicating orally the
                    manifest advantages to the Government of Guatemala which would accrue from a
                    settlement of the Guatemalan debt question. You should be particularly careful
                    not to give the impression that the Government of the United States is
                    intervening in any way in this controversy or that it is trying to bring any
                    pressure on the Government of Guatemala.</p>
                <p>In view of the terms of the 1913 agreement,<anchor n="5" xml:id="d44-f3"/> the
                    Department would not be inclined to support the pending proposals of the
                    bondholders. The Department is mailing to you for your information a detailed
                    history and analysis of the matter which was prepared in the Department.<anchor
                        n="6" xml:id="d44-f4"/> [End paraphrase.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
